The original is already minimal, so the gain here is small. This version compares in `size_t` and uses `data()` plus an offset, which avoids the `operator[]` call and the implicit `uint16` promotion. Behavior is unchanged: the same element is returned for every index, and `FIT_NULL` is returned when the index is out of range.

```cpp
Field* Mesg::GetFieldByIndex(const FIT_UINT16 index)
{
    const size_t i = static_cast<size_t>(index);
    if (i < fields.size())
        return fields.data() + i;

    return FIT_NULL;
}
```